# Redis Official Docs Are the Single Source of Truth

This is a customer-facing demo for Securities & Trading Firm. Anything we **show**,
**claim**, or **configure** in this repo MUST exist in the official Redis
documentation. If it doesn't, the customer will (rightly) say
*"that won't work in production"* — and the deal goes cold.

## The rule

Before adding or modifying any RDI feature, API endpoint, YAML key,
transformation block, JMESPath function, or product claim, **check that
it appears in the official docs**:

| Surface | Authoritative URL |
|---|---|
| RDI overview / features | <https://redis.io/docs/latest/integrate/redis-data-integration/> |
| RDI architecture | <https://redis.io/docs/latest/integrate/redis-data-integration/architecture/> |
| `config.yaml` schema | <https://redis.io/docs/latest/integrate/redis-data-integration/reference/config-yaml-reference/> |
| Job files / transforms | <https://redis.io/docs/latest/integrate/redis-data-integration/data-pipelines/transform-examples/> |
| Data transformation blocks | <https://redis.io/docs/latest/integrate/redis-data-integration/reference/data-transformation/> |
| JMESPath custom functions | <https://redis.io/docs/latest/integrate/redis-data-integration/reference/jmespath-custom-functions/> |
| Control-plane API | <https://redis.io/docs/latest/integrate/redis-data-integration/reference/api-reference/> |
| CLI (`redis-di`) | <https://redis.io/docs/latest/integrate/redis-data-integration/reference/cli/> |
| Redis Enterprise | <https://redis.io/docs/latest/operate/rs/> |
| RedisJSON / RediSearch | <https://redis.io/docs/latest/develop/data-types/json/>, <https://redis.io/docs/latest/develop/interact/search-and-query/> |

## What this means in practice

- **YAML keys** in `rdi/config.yaml` and `rdi/jobs/*.yaml` must be on the
  current schema. If the schema marks a key *DEPRECATED*, replace or
  remove it — do not perpetuate it just because the demo "works".
- **JMESPath functions** must be either in the RDI custom-functions list
  or the [JMESPath builtins](https://jmespath.org/proposals/functions.html).
- **API endpoints** added to `mock-rdi-api/app.py` must mirror a real
  `/api/v1/...` operation; do not invent endpoints Insight could not
  call against production RDI.
- **Slide / talk-track / runbook claims** (throughput, HA, DLQ,
  backpressure, supported sources, etc.) must cite an official doc page.
- **Reference implementations** (`rdi-processor/`, `mock-rdi-api/`) may
  implement *less* than the official product but must never implement
  *more* — i.e. never expose a knob the real product doesn't have.

## When in doubt

1. Read the relevant doc page above first.
2. Cross-check with [`docs/05-rdi-spec-conformance.md`](../../docs/05-rdi-spec-conformance.md)
   — the current spec-conformance audit lists every construct in use.
3. If you genuinely cannot find the feature in the official docs,
   **don't add it**. Flag it to the demo owner instead.

After any change to `rdi/`, `mock-rdi-api/`, slides, or talk-track,
update `docs/05-rdi-spec-conformance.md` and re-run
`./scripts/verify-redis-enterprise.sh` to keep the assurance pack honest.
